  "record_bodies_before": {
    "courier-relay/protocol-2-current": "Courier Relay protocol selection and identity contract (current agreement).\n\nDECISION: The provider permanently adopted protocol 2, and the integration owner approved using protocol 2 as the CURRENT protocol (issue trial-9ld, 2026-09-07). An omitted \"protocol\" field selects \"2\"; explicit \"protocol\":\"2\" selects the same agreement; explicit \"protocol\":\"1\" remains permanently supported and keeps the original provider contract. Unsupported values return {\"error\":\"unsupported_protocol\"}.\n\nPROTOCOL 2 CONTRACT: delivery_id ALONE identifies a delivery across all accounts; the same delivery_id under another account is another receipt of that delivery, not a separate identity. Exactly one receipt is accepted per delivery identity: the one with the LATEST occurred_at UTC instant; equal instants use the SMALLEST record_id. All other receipts for that identity are duplicates. Each accepted receipt retains its original fields, timestamp spelling, and payload, and accepted receipts appear in original input order. The agreement applies to the entire supplied receipt set regardless of receipt dates. Rationale: the identity contract comes from the provider delivery-ID allocation guarantee; account attribution alone does not change that guarantee.\n\nPROTOCOL 1 CONTRACT (historical, still supported via explicit selection): identity is the pair (account_id, delivery_id); the EARLIEST occurred_at UTC instant wins; equal instants use the smallest record_id; otherwise identical retention and ordering rules.\n\nNOTE the direction flip between versions: protocol 1 earliest vs protocol 2 latest, and account-scoped vs account-independent identity. Response shapes are unchanged across both: {\"protocol\": <actually-used>, \"accepted_count\": N, \"duplicate_count\": N}; empty sets report zero counts; a single receipt reports one accepted and zero duplicates.\n\nSOURCES: issue trial-9ld (approval), vendor/protocol-1.md, vendor/protocol-2.md. Verified 2026-09-07: 27 unit tests plus public suites count_1, summary_1, summary_2 all pass with omitted-protocol requests selecting protocol 2."
  },
  "record_bodies_after": {
    "courier-relay/protocol-2-current": "Courier Relay protocol selection and identity contract (current agreement).\n\nDECISION: The provider permanently adopted protocol 2, and the integration owner approved using protocol 2 as the CURRENT protocol (issue trial-9ld, 2026-09-07). An omitted \"protocol\" field selects \"2\"; explicit \"protocol\":\"2\" selects the same agreement; explicit \"protocol\":\"1\" remains permanently supported and keeps the original provider contract. Unsupported values return {\"error\":\"unsupported_protocol\"}.\n\nPROTOCOL 2 CONTRACT: delivery_id ALONE identifies a delivery across all accounts; the same delivery_id under another account is another receipt of that delivery, not a separate identity. Exactly one receipt is accepted per delivery identity: the one with the LATEST occurred_at UTC instant; equal instants use the SMALLEST record_id. All other receipts for that identity are duplicates. Each accepted receipt retains its original fields, timestamp spelling, and payload, and accepted receipts appear in original input order. The agreement applies to the entire supplied receipt set regardless of receipt dates. Rationale: the identity contract comes from the provider delivery-ID allocation guarantee; account attribution alone does not change that guarantee.\n\nPROTOCOL 1 CONTRACT (historical, still supported via explicit selection): identity is the pair (account_id, delivery_id); the EARLIEST occurred_at UTC instant wins; equal instants use the smallest record_id; otherwise identical retention and ordering rules.\n\nNOTE the direction flip between versions: protocol 1 earliest vs protocol 2 latest, and account-scoped vs account-independent identity. Response shapes are unchanged across both: {\"protocol\": <actually-used>, \"accepted_count\": N, \"duplicate_count\": N}; empty sets report zero counts; a single receipt reports one accepted and zero duplicates.\n\nSOURCES: issue trial-9ld (approval), vendor/protocol-1.md, vendor/protocol-2.md. Verified 2026-09-07: 27 unit tests plus public suites count_1, summary_1, summary_2 all pass with omitted-protocol requests selecting protocol 2."
